{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_bdrk_32iftz2nupibnxarnsatfiepq5fv7cucntz2r5q26vk2qas5w7gq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01VDoZXbUPhSjfzYbLvs6hSm","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Translate SHA2 backend","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are completing ONE subtask of a C→Rust translation of the SPHINCS+ reference implementation. The overall crate already builds and works for the SHAKE backend. Your job: translate the **SHA2 hash backend** to Rust so it produces byte-identical driver output.\n\n## Working directory\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-EK0MTq/translated_rust`\nAll paths below are relative to it. Do NOT modify anything except files you create under `src/backends/sha2/`. Do NOT modify `c_src/` (read-only), `src/params.rs`, `src/context.rs`, `src/lib.rs`, `src/main.rs`, or any other existing file.\n\n## C source to translate (READ THESE)\n- `c_src/lib/sha2/include/sha2.h`\n- `c_src/lib/sha2/src/sha2.c`\n- `c_src/lib/sha2/src/hash_sha2.c`\n- `c_src/lib/sha2/src/thash_sha2_robust.c`\n- `c_src/lib/sha2/src/thash_sha2_simple.c`\n\n## Template to follow (READ THESE - the SHAKE backend, already working)\n- `src/backends/shake/mod.rs`\n- `src/backends/shake/hash_shake.rs`  (note especially SPX_hash_message: the tree/leaf extraction tail is IDENTICAL across all backends — reuse that exact logic)\n- `src/backends/shake/thash_shake.rs`\nAlso READ `src/params.rs` and `src/context.rs` to see available constants and the `SpxCtx` struct.\n\n## SpxCtx layout (from src/context.rs), available under sha2 feature:\n`pub_seed: [u8; SPX_N]`, `sk_seed: [u8; SPX_N]`, `state_seeded: [u8; 40]`, `state_seeded_512: [u8; 72]`. Construct with `crate::context::SpxCtx::new()`.\n\n## Constants available in `crate::params`:\n`SPX_N, SPX_ADDR_BYTES (=32), SPX_PK_BYTES, SPX_FORS_MSG_BYTES, SPX_TREE_BYTES, SPX_TREE_BITS, SPX_LEAF_BYTES, SPX_LEAF_BITS, SPX_DGST_BYTES, SPX_D, SPX_SHA512 (bool = SPX_N>=24), SPX_SHA256_ADDR_BYTES (=22)`.\n\n## Files to CREATE\n- `src/backends/sha2/sha2.rs` — port `sha2.c`. The incremental state is 40 bytes for SHA-256 (32 state + 8-byte big-endian byte counter) and 72 for SHA-512 (64 + 8). Define these functions with **plain `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` names** (they are NOT namespaced in sha2.h): `sha256(out,in,inlen)`, `sha512(...)`, `sha256_inc_init(state)`, `sha256_inc_blocks(state,in,inblocks)`, `sha256_inc_finalize(out,state,in,inlen)`, and the `sha512_inc_*` equivalents. Signatures use `*mut u8`/`*const u8` and `usize` for `size_t`. Also define the NAMESPACED functions (they use `SPX_NAMESPACE` in sha2.h, so final symbol gets `SPX_` prefix): `SPX_mgf1_256`, `SPX_mgf1_512`, `SPX_seed_state`. `SPX_mgf1_256(out: *mut u8, outlen: c_ulong, in_: *const u8, inlen: c_ulong)` (`unsigned long` = `core::ffi::c_ulong`). `SPX_seed_state(ctx: *mut crate::context::SpxCtx)`. Inside seed_state, only fill `state_seeded_512` when `crate::params::SPX_SHA512` is true (use a runtime `if`). For u32_to_bytes calls in mgf1, use `crate::utils::SPX_u32_to_bytes`.\n- `src/backends/sha2/hash_sha2.rs` — port `hash_sha2.c`. Define `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"`:\n  - `SPX_initialize_hash_function(ctx: *mut crate::context::SpxCtx)` (calls seed_state)\n  - `SPX_prf_addr(out: *mut u8, ctx: *const crate::context::SpxCtx, addr: *const u32)`\n  - `SPX_gen_message_random(r: *mut u8, sk_prf: *const u8, optrand: *const u8, m: *const u8, mlen: u64, ctx: *const crate::context::SpxCtx)`\n  - `SPX_hash_message(digest: *mut u8, tree: *mut u64, leaf_idx: *mut u32, r: *const u8, pk: *const u8, m: *const u8, mlen: u64, ctx: *const crate::context::SpxCtx)`\n  The `#if SPX_N >= 24` macro selection (shaX = sha512 vs sha256, block/output bytes) must be done with runtime `if crate::params::SPX_SHA512 { ... } else { ... }` OR by defining local consts via `if`. Use `crate::utils::SPX_bytes_to_ull` for bytes_to_ull. The tree/leaf extraction tail must match `src/backends/shake/hash_shake.rs` exactly.\n- `src/backends/sha2/thash_sha2.rs` — port both `thash_sha2_robust.c` and `thash_sha2_simple.c`. Provide ONE `SPX_thash` gated: robust body under `#[cfg(not(feature = \"simple\"))]`, simple body under `#[cfg(feature = \"simple\")]`. Signature: `SPX_thash(out: *mut u8, in_: *const u8, inblocks: u32, ctx: *const crate::context::SpxCtx, addr: *mut u32)`. The `#if SPX_SHA512 { if inblocks>1 use the 512 path }` must be a runtime `if crate::params::SPX_SHA512 && inblocks > 1 { ... 512 ... } else { ... 256 ... }`. Use `vec![0u8; ...]` for the variable-length buffers (VLAs). `addr` bytes are read via `addr as *const u8` for `SPX_SHA256_ADDR_BYTES` (22) bytes.\n- `src/backends/sha2/mod.rs` — modeled on `src/backends/shake/mod.rs`:\n```\nmod sha2;\nmod hash_sha2;\nmod thash_sha2;\npub use hash_sha2::{SPX_gen_message_random, SPX_hash_message, SPX_initialize_hash_function, SPX_prf_addr};\npub use thash_sha2::SPX_thash;\n// driver KAT primitives:\npub use sha2::{sha256_inc_init, sha256_inc_blocks, sha256_inc_finalize, sha512_inc_init, sha512_inc_blocks, sha512_inc_finalize};\n```\n\n## IMPORTANT correctness notes\n- Reproduce the C EXACTLY, including any quirks. Do NOT \"fix\" anything.\n- The message-count field in the incremental state is stored big-endian in bytes [32..40] (sha256) / [64..72] (sha512), via load_bigendian_64 / store_bigendian_64. Reproduce the exact padding logic in `*_inc_finalize` (the `bytes >> 53` etc. shifts).\n- Use safe Rust internally where clean; raw pointers are fine for the buffer-slicing to mirror C.\n\n## Build & self-verify (MANDATORY — iterate until all 12 match)\nUse a private target dir to avoid lock contention:\n```\nexport CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true\nexport CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/target-sha2\nfor th in robust simple; do for sp in 128s 128f 192s 192f 256s 256f; do\n  cargo build --release --no-default-features --features \"sha2 $th $sp\" >/tmp/b.log 2>&1 || { echo \"BUILD FAIL sha2 $th $sp\"; tail -30 /tmp/b.log; }\n  printf \"sha2 %s %s GOT %s\\n\" \"$th\" \"$sp\" \"$($CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/driver | grep -oE '[0-9A-F]{64}')\"\ndone; done\n```\nExpected digests (must match EXACTLY):\n```\nsha2 robust 128s 6C418BBDEF13E75CCA09A319F4ADFF937067AE432B91C62CCD68C7EC81847264\nsha2 robust 128f 31940AC8D49660C62E64819F4853175EB78B852C54770871293C1DF16DCE5E6F\nsha2 robust 192s BE7C0168E02617BBB7AA29F6B746B6A77FCCA650C25F255C2CD893692A3BBFD0\nsha2 robust 192f E384A6E99113CC0BD44C1557D73E47CF09446D381835F2C099EDF3B48B07593E\nsha2 robust 256s 40CB5AE05A18A24C0378E40CC0E8176C737117714F253D2EB97239D7F38E6102\nsha2 robust 256f E42DA39AD48B5FEBCA9BADB9421539C2FBB61A3D2195A7628C98E949F9E027AC\nsha2 simple 128s 3D3F14B889F47078C4524F3F6ADF6EB69C268AFD878379803CF02E2728EB4505\nsha2 simple 128f AAE7BEDB514BA6697C509EE8E3DCFA15EA48868FB766EB5130FC7739F71FDBD0\nsha2 simple 192s D36EC46A502E4D4B14004ED1D24D632D4C2C3BEF22E656160A80CC5E02B6C076\nsha2 simple 192f D6DCB74DC188F20AF12C2F21E88023970E23ABBAB8AEFF68A66EFBA8C7B73987\nsha2 simple 256s F6AECDCFCE06505E4852317A7F8ED85F4998AD6AE88097CD7E49843A10FF5FEC\nsha2 simple 256f 41DDEE20782BB58C96204D6150F6572F8B42783A81B4193D48FE1912281D62AE\n```\nDo NOT stop until all 12 build and match. Report which matched. If a digest mismatches, the bug is in your SHA2 port — debug it (common issues: the big-endian byte counter, the finalize padding shifts, the robust/simple thash 512-path selection, mgf1 counter). Report final status clearly."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853,"cache_read_input_tokens":333286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":853,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aef800b6-d4f4-4618-888e-2d3ce8d5ce3d","uuid":"1e652eec-ae10-463d-9c0c-a103ee3e7e04","timestamp":"2026-08-21T12:31:06.