export SPX_ funcs under unprefixed names main.rs expects):\npub use haraka::{\n    SPX_tweak_constants as tweak_constants,\n    SPX_haraka_S_inc_init as haraka_S_inc_init,\n    SPX_haraka_S_inc_absorb as haraka_S_inc_absorb,\n    SPX_haraka_S_inc_finalize as haraka_S_inc_finalize,\n    SPX_haraka_S_inc_squeeze as haraka_S_inc_squeeze,\n};\n```\n\n## IMPORTANT\n- Reproduce C EXACTLY, do NOT fix bugs. The bit-sliced AES S-box and permutation must be transcribed carefully. The `haraka512_perm` uses the per-round \"Mix states\" bit-permutation constants — copy them exactly.\n- The 128f/128s parameter sets use SPX_N=16 (haraka always uses haraka256/haraka512/haraka_S regardless of N; there is no 512-variant switch for haraka).\n\n## Build & self-verify (MANDATORY — iterate until all 12 match)\nNote: haraka is selected when NO other backend feature is set; pass the `haraka` feature explicitly (it doesn't enable sha2/shake/blake, so the haraka backend module compiles). Use a private target dir:\n```\nexport CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true\nexport CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/target-haraka\nfor th in robust simple; do for sp in 128s 128f 192s 192f 256s 256f; do\n  cargo build --release --no-default-features --features \"haraka $th $sp\" >/tmp/bh.log 2>&1 || { echo \"BUILD FAIL haraka $th $sp\"; tail -30 /tmp/bh.log; }\n  printf \"haraka %s %s GOT %s\\n\" \"$th\" \"$sp\" \"$($CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/driver | grep -oE '[0-9A-F]{64}')\"\ndone; done\n```\nExpected digests (must match EXACTLY):\n```\nharaka robust 128s 83F5A066568F19984AC55D5ECBFB2C6E935482CE204EF802AD408C3CAFCFD532\nharaka robust 128f C66C9958C3F9989D9327919E5C20F21CF89555E1E8F7441CDEC5C05BB67E2E4C\nharaka robust 192s DC65C19610F816013BA0473AC17E809A555EBE7E62CFC263AAEDCB2C7B34B37D\nharaka robust 192f 861B571B1B9CE8C5C2E655FAA0859A580218E0293E08FB6A76D35561BB202847\nharaka robust 256s 1D12953509F85B0CBD6C16C3A9A057E4A2990B8ED06437F8597BB12266A7F9FC\nharaka robust 256f CA95D5AAE9089402E7B3F86CB5784FC9738D1048EB214AE5B9B482C