ot `blake256(out,in,inlen)` wrapper calls `blake256_update(&S, in, inlen*8)`. Reproduce EXACTLY as written in the C (blake update interprets datalen as bits; do not \"fix\"). tree/leaf tail identical to shake.\n- `src/backends/blake/thash_blake.rs` — port `thash_blake_robust.c` and `thash_blake_simple.c` into one `SPX_thash(out: *mut u8, in_: *const u8, inblocks: u32, ctx: *const crate::context::SpxCtx, addr: *mut u32)`. robust under `#[cfg(not(feature=\"simple\"))]`, simple under `#[cfg(feature=\"simple\")]`. Inside, `if crate::params::SPX_BLAKE512 && inblocks > 1 { 512 path } else { 256 path }`. NOTE in the robust 256 path the C hashes `buf + SPX_N` (skips pub_seed) for the final blake256 — reproduce that exact offset. Use `vec![0u8; ...]` for VLAs. `addr` read via `addr as *const u8` for 32 bytes.\n- `src/backends/blake/mod.rs`:\n```\nmod blake256;\nmod blake512;\nmod hash_blake;\nmod thash_blake;\npub use hash_blake::{SPX_gen_message_random, SPX_hash_message, SPX_initialize_hash_function, SPX_prf_addr};\npub use thash_blake::SPX_thash;\n// driver KAT primitives:\npub use blake256::{blakestate256, blake256_init, blake256_update, blake256_final};\npub use blake512::{blakestate512, blake512_init, blake512_update, blake512_final};\n```\n\n## IMPORTANT\n- Reproduce C EXACTLY; do NOT fix bugs. The BLAKE compression ROUND macro is long — transcribe carefully. `blake256_final`/`blake512_final` padding logic (the buflen==440/888 special cases, `S->t[0] -= ...`, nullt) must be exact.\n- `blake256_update`/`blake512_update` take datalen in BITS as in the C; internal `blake256()` multiplies inlen*8; the hash_blake update calls pass byte counts directly (a quirk) — reproduce as written.\n\n## Build & self-verify (MANDATORY — iterate until all 12 match)\n```\nexport CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true\nexport CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$TMPDIR/target-blake\nfor th in robust simple; do for sp in 128s 128f 192s 192f 256s 256f; do\n  cargo build --release --no-default-features --features \"blake $th $sp\" >/tmp/bl.log 2>&1 || { echo \"BUILD FAIL blake $th $sp\"; tail -30 /tmp/bl.log; }\n  printf \"blake %s %s GOT %s\\n\" \"$th\" \"$sp\" \"$($CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/driver | grep -oE '[0-9A-F]{64}')\"\ndone; done\n```\nExpected digests (must match EXACTLY):\n```\nblake robust 128s 373DBB13778DC098915F3C32A7EAF4DE245E0F16F8FB7F5BA46EC6BBFF9D6C21\nblake robust 128f 8B796E297CFB619BF19FFCFA527DD6001FA402DC1E1543BCF097DCAF846775E9\nblake robust 192s A61C8A41B483383CAD120FFC53F1A67F2705D00A7DEAB007E232E922A9FD1CC6\nblake robust 192f 47F429DBFC6328EF47D705EEE9DDC6C57E602287739F7C07481D4C4803C92E44\nblake robust 256s 40D78A429874A9B50A5468CA1D6240D25C30E25E31307C4502AB8F48375D9D98\nblake robust 256f 1E50C04D772C5074B1412181F6A15D5CAAAC2426A5095E00076AB5CF95FA11CE\nblake simple 128s 2DE15917609CA8F8920922BB48B6D1BE80F08DC345BC1FB159592CA697210378\nblake simple 128f 97B452A98F312321D982CDE133B1BF6D7189DC0A9296338C9A823A6689670584\nblake simple 192s 3B22978183DFE5B922D13E3FE8F8D6CCF85C1723C1AD1C55CA25F8962D4C2CFB\nblake simple 192f AF762F4CF491CAF22642E0A9A66C36C15D216CE9B79ECF62A090F7DCA9C12557\nblake simple 256s B78485B5E5748EE2F61B7AFE1735E167D626C1EF24B7858F768B1BC803245A96\nblake simple 256f A152E392DAAAC7FAFBF11AD859D03E7FD37906AEDFB2686F9627116679D24583\n```\nDo NOT stop until all 12 build and match. Report final status clearly.","uuid":"141a8dda-ffa0-4975-92fd-d77a15caed47","session_id":"aef800b6-d4f4-4618-888e-2d3ce8d5ce3d"}
