ha2.rs`**: The C `EXPAND_32`/`EXPAND_64` + `F_32`/`F_64` macro-unrolled compression was verified to be exactly the standard schedule (`W[t] = σ1(W[t-2]) + W[t-7] + σ0(W[t-15]) + W[t-16]`, with the rotating `w0..w15` registers) and implemented as `K_256`/`K_512` tables + 64/80-round loops. All K constants were transcribed from the `F_*` call sites in the C. All adds use `wrapping_add`. Byte counter kept big-endian at `state[32..40]`/`state[64..72]` via faithful `load/store_bigendian_64`; `store_bigendian_32` takes a `u64` argument as in C.\n- Non-namespaced exports (`sha256`, `sha512`, `sha256_inc_*`, `sha512_inc_*`) vs. namespaced (`SPX_mgf1_256`, `SPX_mgf1_512`, `SPX_seed_state`) match `sha2.h`. `SPX_seed_state` only fills `state_seeded_512` under a runtime `if SPX_SHA512`.\n- **`hash_sha2.rs`**: `SPX_SHAX_*` selection is `const`-level (`if SPX_SHA512 {…} else {…}` is const-evaluable since `SPX_SHA512` is a `const bool`), so `buf`/`state`/`inbuf` stay fixed-size arrays; the primitive dispatch itself is via small runtime-`if` wrappers (`shaX_inc_init`, `shaX_inc_blocks`, `shaX_inc_finalize`, `shaX`, `mgf1_X`). `SPX_INBLOCKS` reproduces the `& -BLOCK` power-of-2 rounding as `& !(BLOCK-1)`. The tree/leaf extraction tail is character-for-character the same logic as `hash_shake.rs`.\n- **`thash_sha2.rs`**: One `SPX_thash` per THASH variant via `#[cfg(feature = \"simple\")]` / `#[cfg(not(...))]`, each dispatching to a private `thash_512` under `if SPX_SHA512 && inblocks > 1`. VLAs became `vec![0u8; …]`.\n- **C quirk preserved**: in the robust 256-bit path, `buf` is sized `SPX_N + SPX_SHA256_OUTPUT_BYTES (32) + inblocks*SPX_N` while the address is only 22 bytes and writes start at offset `SPX_N + 22` — i.e. the C over-allocates by 10 bytes. I kept the C's sizing expression rather than \"fixing\" it to `SPX_SHA256_ADDR_BYTES` (the 512 path in the same file does use 22, and both are correct because 22 < 32).\n\nThe `shake` backend was re-checked afterward and still produces its expected digest (`B4417E77…`), confirming no cross-backend regression."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":100843,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":807,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VDoZXbUPhSjfzYbLvs6hSm","session_id":"aef800b6-d4f4-4618-888e-2d3ce8d5ce3d","uuid":"e61ad0ad-3bc4-4b63-a249-bb6620d7bb78","timestamp":"2026-08-21T12:45:35.407Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate SHA2 backend"}
