yte-counter semantics exactly, including the post-loop use of the loop counter `i` in `_squeeze` (transcribed as `while` loops) and wrapping u8 arithmetic on the counter.\n- `hash_message` absorbs `pk + SPX_N` (root only), as in the C — not the full `SPX_PK_BYTES` like the SHAKE backend; the tree/leaf extraction tail is identical to shake.\n- The `memset(buf_tmp, 0, 64)` in both `thash` variants is satisfied by the declaration's zero-init (commented), which removed the only compiler warning; `SPX_haraka256` is imported only for the robust build.\n\n## Verification\nAll 12 configurations (`robust`/`simple` x `128s/128f/192s/192f/256s/256f`, built with `--no-default-features --features \"haraka <thash> <secpar>\"`) build with **zero warnings** and the driver output diffs clean against the expected digest list — `ALL 12 MATCH`.\n\nOne environment caveat: a concurrent agent (the BLAKE subtask) is sharing `$TMPDIR` and initially clobbered my results file with its own lines; I re-ran with PID-unique temp filenames to get the clean result above. Only the four `src/backends/haraka/*.rs` files were created by me; no pre-existing file was modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":93107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":683,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01X1JSsS6eiusL29rM2QUuKU","session_id":"aef800b6-d4f4-4618-888e-2d3ce8d5ce3d","uuid":"38202d3f-603d-46a2-b338-a40bf68d7a15","timestamp":"2026-08-21T12:48:08.191Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate Haraka backend"}
